IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `twa-dates`
IMPORT `twa-rules`
IMPORT `twa-seat`

-- Wills Act 2008 (Tas) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (twa-seat.l4), the date helpers (twa-dates.l4) and
-- the rules (twa-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the
-- encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `dates`

#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 10 4 2025
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 31 1 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 30 `days after` (`d` 15 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 16 3 2024

§§ `s 6 -- what the will can give`

#ASSERT `Could the will give away this property` `property the will-maker was entitled to at death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could the will give away this property` `property the personal representative became entitled to, as personal representative, after the death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could the will give away this property` `property the will-maker held as trustee at death` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 7, 8, 11, 20, 60 -- was the will validly made`

-- Arguments: age; married; in contemplation of a marriage; it took place; under a s 20 order; Registrar a witness;
-- within the order's conditions; minor valid elsewhere; in writing; signed; meant to execute; witnesses present
-- together; witnesses who could see and signed; conforms to a s 60 law.
-- An adult, signed before 2 witnesses present together who both signed.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 3 witnesses present, 2 of them signed: enough.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 3 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 present but only 1 could see and signed (the other blind, s 11, or never signed): not valid.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The witnesses came one at a time: never 2 present together.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Signed, but not meaning to execute it (s 8(2)).
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only 1 witness, but it conforms to the law of the place where it was signed (s 60).
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Age: 17 is a minor, 18 is not.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A married minor.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A married minor whose will was not properly witnessed.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In contemplation of a marriage that took place, and one that did not.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 16 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 16 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Court-authorised will: the Registrar a witness, conditions kept; without the Registrar; outside the conditions.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A deceased minor's will valid where he or she lived (s 20(5)), though not witnessed as s 8 requires.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 60 saves the form, not the age.
#ASSERT `Was the will validly made` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 10 -- an informal document`

#ASSERT `Can the document count as the will` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the document count as the will` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the document count as the will` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 12 -- a gift to a witness`

-- Two witnesses, one of them me.
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 2 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Three witnesses, two independent: saved (s 12(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 3 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Three witnesses, but the other two are a beneficiary and a beneficiary's spouse: only one independent.
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 3 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Exactly 2 witnesses can never save the gift under (a): "more than 2".
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 2 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 2 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I attested the will` 2 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I claim under a person who attested the will` 2 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- My spouse witnessed, I did not: s 12(1) voids only the witness's own gift (finding 2).
#ASSERT `Is my gift void because I witnessed the will` `I neither attested the will nor claim under a person who did` 2 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 13, 14 -- keeping a gift as a witness`

#ASSERT `By when must I apply to keep my gift as a witness` (`d` 15 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 7 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to keep my gift as a witness` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
-- Arguments: grant made; grant day; application day; finally distributed; extension; knew and approved; no fraud.
-- The last day of the 6 months, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 15 7 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 16 7 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 16 7 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No application after the final distribution, even with an extension, even within the 6 months.
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 16 7 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before any grant; and an application made before a grant that came later.
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 2 1 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- In time, but the Court is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Grant on 31 August 2025: the 6 months end on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court let me keep my gift as a witness` TRUE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 15 -- revocation`

#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `a later will revoked it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `a writing declaring an intention to revoke it was executed as a will must be` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `a document the Court accepts under section 10 revoked it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `a Court order for a minor or for a person lacking capacity revoked it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `the will-maker burnt, tore or otherwise destroyed it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Torn up by accident: no intention.
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `the will-maker burnt, tore or otherwise destroyed it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `another person burnt, tore or destroyed it in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Destroyed by someone else out of the will-maker's presence, even at his or her wish.
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `another person burnt, tore or destroyed it, not in the will-maker's presence or not at his or her direction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `the will-maker, or another person in his or her presence and at his or her direction, wrote on it or dealt with it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `the will-maker, or another person in his or her presence and at his or her direction, wrote on it or dealt with it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `the will-maker's circumstances changed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the will been revoked` `nothing was done to it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 -- marriage`

-- Arguments: married after the will; I am the spouse at death; power of appointment; this marriage contemplated;
-- marriage generally contemplated.
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The new spouse keeps his or her gift and appointments.
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the marriage revoke the will as to my benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 17 -- divorce`

#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `an appointment as executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `an appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include my children` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `a power of appointment exercisable by me or in my favour` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `a power of appointment exercisable by me only in favour of children of whom the will-maker and I are both parents` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` TRUE `a gift of property` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A will made after the divorce.
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975` FALSE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `the Family Court granted a decree of nullity` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `it was dissolved or annulled outside Australia and that is recognised in Australia` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `it was dissolved or annulled outside Australia and that is not recognised in Australia` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `our registered deed of relationship was revoked under the Relationships Act 2003` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Separated but not divorced at the death (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `we separated but the marriage was not dissolved` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `an unregistered significant relationship ended` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the end of our relationship revoke what the will gives me` `it has not ended` TRUE `a gift of property` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 18 -- alterations`

#ASSERT `Does the change on the will count` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the alteration counts as part of the will`
#ASSERT `Does the change on the will count` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the alteration counts as part of the will`
#ASSERT `Does the change on the will count` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the alteration counts as part of the will`
#ASSERT `Does the change on the will count` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the alteration does not count and the will reads as before`
#ASSERT `Does the change on the will count` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the original words are gone, but nothing written in their place counts`

§§ `s 19 -- revival`

#ASSERT `Has the revoked will been revived` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the revoked will been revived` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the revoked will been revived` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 31 -- a statutory will made by the Tribunal`

#ASSERT `Is the Tribunal's statutory will valid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Tribunal's statutory will valid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the Tribunal's statutory will valid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 42 -- rectification`

#ASSERT `By when must I apply to rectify the will` (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 10 4 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to rectify the will` (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to rectify the will` (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
-- Arguments: death; application day; finally distributed; extension; reason; satisfied.
-- The last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 4 2025) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 4 2025) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 4 2025) FALSE TRUE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 4 2025) TRUE TRUE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A final distribution within the 3 months does not stop an application made in time (finding 7).
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 4 2025) TRUE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE `another reason` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court rectify the will on my application` (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 42(4). Arguments: s 64 distribution; knew of an application; death; distribution day.
#ASSERT `Is the personal representative protected for the distribution` TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 20 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On the last day of the 3 months a distribution is protected though an application that day is in time (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Is the personal representative protected for the distribution` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the personal representative protected for the distribution` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 9 4 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the personal representative protected for the distribution` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 49 -- 30 days' survival`

#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 31 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 2 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 10 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Across 29 February 2024: day 30 after 15 February is 16 March.
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2024) (`d` 16 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the gift fail because the beneficiary died within 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2024) (`d` 17 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 45 -- failed gifts to residue`

#ASSERT `Does the failed gift fall into the residue` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the failed gift fall into the residue` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the failed gift fall into the residue` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 55 -- the issue take the share`

-- Arguments: OB is issue; interest lasts; gift to issue generally; will-maker's death; OB's death; I would share on an
-- intestacy; I survived 30 days; condition failed; contrary intention.
-- The original beneficiary died a month before the will-maker.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Died on the 30th day after: did not survive for 30 days.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 31 1 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Died on the 31st day: survived, so the share goes to his or her own estate.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A gift to a nephew, not the will-maker's issue.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A life interest.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A grandchild whose own parent is alive would not share on the intestacy.
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I take the share in place of the original beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 56(2) -- a failed fraction`

-- A half, a quarter and a quarter; one quarter fails: the half becomes two thirds, the other quarter one third.
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` 0.5 1 0.25 FALSE EQUALS JUST (2 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` 0.25 1 0.25 FALSE EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- Thirds; one fails: a half each.
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) 1 (1 DIVIDED BY 3) FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.5
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` 0.5 1 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.5
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` 0.5 1 0.25 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What fraction do I take after another fails` 0.5 1 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 63 -- seeing the will`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` FALSE `I am named or referred to in it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am named or referred to in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am the will-maker's surviving spouse` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am a parent or guardian of the will-maker` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am the will-maker's child or other issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I would share in the estate on an intestacy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am a creditor or have another claim against the estate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am a beneficiary under an earlier will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `I am a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or who would share on an intestacy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to inspect and copy the will` TRUE `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING

